[Term]
id: CL:4301312
name: SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_3 substantia nigra dopaminergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A substantia nigra dopaminergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a3 (Mmus), Aldh1a7 (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0882 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Midbrain (MB; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter dopamine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: BG group. Refined via MapMyCells crosswalk to HMBA basal ganglia group 'SN-VTR CALB1 Dopa' (CS20250428), whose CL term has parent substantia nigra dopaminergic neuron; to be re-checked against the original MapMyCells output. Other inferred CL parents: midbrain dopaminergic neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_3 does not have cells in midbrain raphe nuclei (RAmb). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
