[Term]
id: CL:4301313
name: SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_4 midbrain dopaminergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A midbrain dopaminergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of 9030622O22Rik (Mmus), Cd44 (Mmus), Klhl14 (Mmus), Lepr (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0883 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Midbrain (MB; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter dopamine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: region+NT. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_4 does not have cells in substantia nigra, compact part (SNc). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. {xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z", xref="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9"}
