[Term]
id: CL:4301575
name: Lugaro cell (Mmus)
def: "A Lugaro cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pthlh (Mmus), Tfap2b (Mmus), Rspo2 (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:1145 CB PLI Gly-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17543831]
comment: Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Mapping of this cell type is supported by high target purity (~98%) and consistent GABA–glycine neurotransmitter predictions and neurotransmitter agreement. Mapping of this cell type is corroborated by MapMyCells-based bioinformatic analysis of Osorno et al. 2022 and its spatial localization profile. Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. {xref="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17543831"}
