[Term]
id: CL:4302146
name: L2 IT PPP-APr Glut_3 Trpv6 L2 intratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A L2 intratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Teddm3 (Mmus), Smoc2 (Mmus), Rmst (Mmus), Galr1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other L2 IT PPP-APr Glut_3 cells by expression of Trpv6, Pcdh17. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, Retrohippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Postsubiculum, Dentate gyrus, molecular layer, Presubiculum . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0326 L2 IT PPP-APr Glut_3." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
