[Term]
id: CL:4302168
name: L4 RSP-ACA Glut_1 Pvalb cerebral cortex neuron (Mmus)
def: "A cerebral cortex neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Scnn1a (Mmus), Cbln1 (Mmus), Vsig2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other L4 RSP-ACA Glut cells by expression of Pvalb. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Isocortex , in or close to the regions: Retrosplenial area, ventral part, layer 2/3, Retrosplenial area, ventral part, layer 5 . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0348 L4 RSP-ACA Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
