[Term]
id: CL:4302219
name: CA2-FC-IG Glut_1 hippocampal CA1-3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A hippocampal CA1-3 neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lefty1 (Mmus), Tmem215 (Mmus), Fgf16 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CA2-FC-IG Glut cells by expression of Slc9a4. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Aldh1a1). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region , in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum oriens, Field CA1, pyramidal layer, Field CA3, stratum oriens . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0399 CA2-FC-IG Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, CA2-FC-IG Glut_1 does not have cells in fasciola cinerea (FC), induseum griseum (IG). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
