[Term]
id: CL:4302317
name: HPF CR Glut_1 Rspo3 Cajal-Retzius cell (Mmus)
def: "A Cajal-Retzius cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Trp73 (Mmus), Shisal2b (Mmus), Creb5 (Mmus), Gdf5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other HPF CR Glut cells by expression of Rspo3, Cdkn1c. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hippocampal region, Retrohippocampal region, brain , in or close to the regions: Dentate gyrus, molecular layer, Field CA1, stratum lacunosum-moleculare . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0497 HPF CR Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
