[Term]
id: CL:4302747
name: PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_1 Rxfp1 GABA-Chol neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABA-Chol neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc18a3 (Mmus), Dsg1a (Mmus), Gbx1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_1 cells by expression of Rxfp1. It is cholinergic (inferred from expression of Chat, Slc18a3, Slc18a2, Slc17a8, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Pallidum, brain , in or close to the regions: Globus pallidus, external segment, Substantia innominata, Diagonal band nucleus, internal capsule . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:0927 PAL-STR Gaba-Chol_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
