[Term]
id: CL:4303276
name: SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_6 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nup62cl (Mmus), Npffr2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba cells by expression of Gm31938. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral preoptic area . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1456 SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_6." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SI-MPO-LPO Lhx8 Gaba_6 does not have cells in substantia innominata (SI), medial preoptic area (MPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
