[Term]
id: CL:4303396
name: TMv-PMv Tbx3 Hist-Gaba_1 Crhbp histaminergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A histaminergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Hdc (Mmus), Ccn5 (Mmus), Dsp (Mmus). It is distinguished from other TMv-PMv Tbx3 Hist-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Crhbp. It is histaminergic (inferred from expression of Hdc, Slc18a2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus , in or close to the regions: Lateral hypothalamic area, Tuberal nucleus, Dorsomedial nucleus of the hypothalamus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1576 TMv-PMv Tbx3 Hist-Gaba_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type TMv-PMv Tbx3 Hist-Gaba_1 Crhbp does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for tuberomammillary nucleus, ventral part (TMv), ventral premammillary nucleus (PMv). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
