id: CL:4303809
name: BST-po Iigp1 Glut glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Iigp1 (Mmus), Prkcq (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CNU-HYa Glut cells by expression of Iigp1, Prkcq. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Gad1). These cells are located in the Thalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Anteroventral nucleus of thalamus, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, fimbria . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:1989 BST-po Iigp1 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
