[Term]
id: CL:4304158
name: LHA-AHN-PVH Otp Trh Glut_4 Pappa2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sim2 (Mmus), Pappa2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other LHA-AHN-PVH Otp Trh Glut_4 cells by expression of Pappa2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Ddc, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum , in or close to the regions: Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Dorsomedial nucleus of the hypothalamus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2338 LHA-AHN-PVH Otp Trh Glut_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, LHA-AHN-PVH Otp Trh Glut_4 Pappa2 does not have cells in lateral hypothalamic area (LHA), paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus (PVH). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
