[Term]
id: CL:4304433
name: AD Serpinb7 Glut_1 Has2os glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Eps8l2 (Mmus), C1ql2 (Mmus), Has2os (Mmus). It is distinguished from other AD Serpinb7 Glut cells by expression of Has2os. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Thalamus, brain , in or close to the regions: Anterodorsal nucleus, stria medullaris . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:2613 AD Serpinb7 Glut_1." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
