[Term]
id: CL:4305949
name: PRNc-NI-SG-RPO Vsx2 Nr4a2 Glut_2 Pdgfd glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Vsx2 (Mmus), Frem3 (Mmus), Pnoc (Mmus), Skor1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRNc-NI-SG-RPO Vsx2 Nr4a2 Glut_2 cells by expression of Pdgfd, Pnoc, Skor1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6, Th). These cells are located in the Pons , in or close to the regions: Abducens nucleus, Superior central nucleus raphe, Pontine central gray . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4129 PRNc-NI-SG-RPO Vsx2 Nr4a2 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PRNc-NI-SG-RPO Vsx2 Nr4a2 Glut_2 Pdgfd does not have cells in supragenual nucleus (SG), nucleus raphe pontis (RPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
