[Term]
id: CL:4306031
name: PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_2 Nr4a2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Evx1os (Mmus), Tcf7l2 (Mmus), Spon1 (Mmus), Zmat4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_2 cells by expression of Nr4a2, Cpne4. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, Pons , in or close to the regions: Gigantocellular reticular nucleus, Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4211 PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, PRP-NI-PRNc-GRN Otp Glut_2 Nr4a2 does not have cells in nucleus prepositus (PRP), nucleus incertus (NI). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
