[Term]
id: CL:4306381
name: VCO Mafa Meis2 Glut_2 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Fshr (Mmus), 2610307P16Rik (Mmus). It is distinguished from other VCO Mafa Meis2 Glut cells by expression of Calb1. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7, Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Medulla, Cerebellum , in or close to the regions: Ventral cochlear nucleus, Flocculus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4561 VCO Mafa Meis2 Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.
