[Term]
id: CL:4306767
name: MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Slc6a2 GABAergic neuron (Mmus)
def: "A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a2 (Mmus), Dmbx1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_2 cells by expression of Slc6a2. It is GABAergic and glycinergic (inferred from expression of Slc6a5, Slc32a1, Slc6a2, Gad2, Gad1). These cells are located in the Medulla, brain , in or close to the regions: choroid plexus, fourth ventricle, Medial vestibular nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:4947 MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_2 Slc6a2 does not have cells in spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV), nucleus prepositus (PRP). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
