[Term]
id: CL:4307021
name: CB Granule Glut_2 Clstn2 cerebellar granule cell (Mmus)
def: "A cerebellar granule cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gabra6 (Mmus), Daam2 (Mmus), Calb2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CB Granule Glut_2 cells by expression of Clstn2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a7). These cells are located in the Cerebellum, brain , in or close to the regions: Simple lobule . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5201 CB Granule Glut_2." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
